ed and the swapped packet streams that Kshana rejects; the CRC of 8 messages and 57 PEC fields equals CPython binascii.crc_hqx and spacepackets-rs 0.18.0 (check value 0x29B1); 66 CUC and CDS time-code cases equal spacepackets-rs 0.18.0 write and read octet for octet (3 CDS cases also spacepackets-py 0.32.0); 4 spacepackets-py 0.32.0 PusTm packets are byte-identical to Kshana's. Not covered: agency-epoch time codes (7 cases rest on unit tests), TC transfer frames and any link layer below the packet</td><td><code>space_packet (TimeCode, SecondaryHeader, packet error control, segmentation and reassembly, stream decoding)</code></td></tr><tr><td>SPICE SPK export (types 9 and 13)</td><td>Writer and reader of NAIF SPICE SPK kernels of types 9 (Lagrange, unequal time steps) and 13 (Hermite, unequal time steps), with the DAF layout, segment descriptors and epoch directories, and the export of a CCSDS OEM to an SPK kernel (UTC or TDB epochs to ephemeris time)</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>CSPICE N0067 through spiceypy 8.3.0, leapseconds kernel naif0012.tls, pre-registered (75bc61d9) before SPICE read any Kshana kernel: SPICE's inventory of Kshana's four kernels is exact; spkpvn and spkgeo at 5 516 epochs and 690 chain evaluations equal Kshana's own evaluation bit for bit and stay inside the bar at every node (worst 0.022 of it); Kshana reads SPICE-written kernels bit-identically; for the same inputs Kshana's kernels are byte-identical to SPICE's (0 differing bytes in four files); OEM epochs convert to ephemeris time within 6.0e-8 s of str2et (bar 1e-6 s) and SPICE evaluates the OEM export inside the bar (worst 0.060). Synthetic Kepler arcs: nothing about physical accuracy. Other SPK types are not written</td><td><code>spk_writer (SpkSegment, to_bytes, from_bytes, eval, et_from_label, oem_to_spk_segments)</code></td></tr><tr><td>SPICE SPK types 3 and 21 (Chebyshev, extended difference lines)</td><td>Writer and reader of NAIF SPICE SPK segments of type 3 (Chebyshev polynomials for