> kind's compose section: named shared values (for example one jammer's power and position) written into each member at the keys it binds them to, every member run, and per metric the smallest, largest and mean value across the members with the member named; metric units must agree across members</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Composition identity against the stand-alone run. The shared-condition arithmetic is bookkeeping; the physics is that of the member kinds, each with its own row</td><td><code>campaign (run_compose)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Bounded optimisation of one metric over campaign parameters</td><td>The <code>campaign</code> kind's optimize section (CAP-32): one to three dotted scenario keys bounded to [lo, hi] on a lin or log scale, one metric read by result path, goal minimize, maximize or target; method grid (the sweep's axis values) or a deterministic Nelder-Mead simplex in normalised coordinates with box projection and the standard coefficients; a missing or non-finite metric scores worst and stays in the trace; with runs &gt; 1 the metric is the mean over common seeds; every evaluation is a real run of the named kind, listed in trace and counted in the reproducibility digest</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Internal only: the exact -20 log10(range) closed form of the link equation, an independent brute-force grid over the same kind, and the Rosenbrock function. Round 1's 1-D bar is NOT MET (the pre-registered box excluded the 3 dB solution; the optimiser stopped at the bound), recorded in docs/design/evidence/cap32-optimize/RESULTS.md and not re-scored. The optimum is local to the box and the start; no global-optimum claim</td><td><code>campaign::optimize (run_optimize, nelder_mead)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Band-limited closed forms for any ranging signal: power in band and early-late code-tracking jitter against published values, with the Gabor bandwidth and offset spectral separation cross-checked</td><td>navsignal: the sine integral (sine_integral), the BPSK-R