 <td>Calibration of the open receiver&#39;s C/N0 and lock models to IQ campaign results, with stated prediction error</td>
 <td>iq::labfit (campaign, cn0, iqfit, iqreport) and <code>[input] campaign</code> on <code>kshana iq labfit</code>, Python <code>kshana.iq_labfit</code> and the MCP labfit tool (campaign folders inside its work directory only): reads a <code>kshana iq campaign</code> output folder by its DIGEST and groups the scored cells into fit units (signal x loop design x front-end chain x jammer type, never pooled). Per unit, it fits measured C/N0 against stated J/S with the spectral-separation form. Q_eff is not identifiable from C/N0 data without an independent measurement of the jammer and signal powers, so Q is stated, never fitted (the type table, the event&#39;s q, or for an unknown type the most damaging stated value, cw Q = 1). The fitted parameter is the identifiable offset delta_eff = delta - 10 log10 Q, with the correlation guard reporting the degeneracy. C/N0 bins locked under 90 % are censored and listed. The threshold J/S is given directly and by the closed form; the tracking-loop and empirical lock models are coupled through the C/N0 model, with drop and re-lock dwells. A seeded cluster bootstrap over recordings (1000 replicates) gives percentile intervals; 90 % prediction intervals come from residual draws; leave-one-recording-out hold-outs are split into interpolation and extrapolation; a pre-registered [validation] table is hashed and each bar judged PASS/FAIL. Report kshana.labfit-iq/1 as JSON, CSV and generated Markdown, with a units block. Synthetic only (no third-party recording, no jammer waveform). The receiver-log labfit path is unchanged</td>
 <td>InternalConsistency</td>
-<td>checked against its own closed-form / analytic identity — catches transcription and coefficient errors, but is not an external oracle — Synthetic parameter recovery on Kshana&#39;s own GPS L1 C/A scenes with a known C/N0 profile imposed from the section 3.1 formula, tracked and scored by kshana iq campaign, against bars pre-registered in docs/design/LABFIT-FROM-IQ.md (section 5.1, amended 2026-10-12 in 4ca3ef3, section 13). The campaigns&#39; C/N0 estimator (M2M4) was fixed in fa388b82, pushed before the first bar evaluation (committed together with the fit code, not alone), after one disclosed diagnostic tracking run. FINDING on the 18-event bar campaign: (c) PASS; (a&#39;) NOT MET, delta_eff error -1.097 dB against 0.5 dB (still -0.89 dB on bins at 38 dB-Hz and above); (b&#39;) NOT MET, 0 of 50 campaigns cover the truth (error -1.189 +/- 0.093 dB, interval about 0.3 dB); (d) NOT MET, closed form 2.20 dB below the direct J/S at loss, about the fitted drop dwell times the ramp rate (2.09 dB); the original Q clauses of (a) and (b) are NOT MET because Q is not identifiable. FOLLOW-UP (bars pre-registered in 99e7c599, docs/design/evidence/labfit-followup/RESULTS.md): on a stepped-J/S campaign delta_eff is recovered within +0.185 dB (S1 MET: the ramp error is estimator lag); (d) as written on it is met by the tracking-loop model (0.45 dB) but not the empirical one (6.42 dB), so S2 is NOT MET; on a fresh ramp campaign (d) with the fitted drop dwell times each event&#39;s ramp rate added is within 1 dB for both models (R1 MET), and (a&#39;) and (d) as written miss again (-1.25 dB; 2.32 and 9.47 dB). The method is checked, not any receiver: it cannot be VALIDATED from synthetic data</td>
+<td>checked against its own closed-form / analytic identity — catches transcription and coefficient errors, but is not an external oracle — Synthetic parameter recovery on Kshana&#39;s own GPS L1 C/A scenes with a known C/N0 profile imposed from the section 3.1 formula, tracked and scored by kshana iq campaign, against bars pre-registered in docs/design/LABFIT-FROM-IQ.md (section 5.1, amended 2026-10-12 in 4ca3ef3, section 13). The campaigns&#39; C/N0 estimator (M2M4) was fixed in fa388b82, pushed before the first bar evaluation (committed together with the fit code, not alone), after one disclosed diagnostic tracking run. FINDING on the 18-event bar campaign: (c) PASS; (a&#39;) NOT MET, delta_eff error -1.097 dB against 0.5 dB (still -0.89 dB on bins at 38 dB-Hz and above); (b&#39;) NOT MET, 0 of 50 campaigns cover the truth (error -1.189 +/- 0.093 dB, interval about 0.3 dB); (d) NOT MET, closed form 2.20 dB below the direct J/S at loss, about the fitted drop dwell times the ramp rate (2.09 dB); the original Q clauses of (a) and (b) are NOT MET because Q is not identifiable. FOLLOW-UP (bars pre-registered in 99e7c599, docs/design/evidence/labfit-followup/RESULTS.md): on a stepped-J/S campaign delta_eff is recovered within +0.185 dB (S1 MET: the ramp error is estimator lag); (d) as written on it is met by the tracking-loop model (0.45 dB) but not the empirical one (6.42 dB), so S2 is NOT MET; on a fresh ramp campaign (d) with the fitted drop dwell times each event&#39;s ramp rate added is within 1 dB for both models (R1 MET), and (a&#39;) and (d) as written miss again (-1.25 dB; 2.32 and 9.47 dB). RE-RUN 0.41 (D8a row 6, 61b389998, docs/design/evidence/d8a-iq-tracking-cn0-rerun/): with the fit modelling each bin 0.5 s earlier along the profile ([campaign_fit] cn0_lag_s), still NOT MET: (a&#39;) +0.5015 dB seen (bar 0.5) and +0.399 dB fresh; (b&#39;) 0 of 50 on seen and fresh seeds, now +0.45 to +0.47 dB with every interval above the truth (the 0.5 s lag overshoots); (c) met on seen seeds, missed on fresh (time-to-loss coverage 1.000 against a bar of at most 0.98); (d) 2.19 dB seen, 0.32 dB fresh. The controls (lag 0) reproduced before scoring (disclosed). A different lag would need a new pre-registration. The method is checked, not any receiver: it cannot be VALIDATED from synthetic data</td>
