M-PKR), the ECDSA P-256/P-521 signature of the DSM-KROOT, TESLA key-chain verification (SHA-256 or SHA3-256), MACSEQ and tag verification (HMAC-SHA-256 or CMAC-AES) for ADKD 0, 4 and 12 with cross-authentication, chain end/revocation/renewal, public-key renewal and revocation, and the alert message; per-satellite status Authenticated/Failed/Unavailable with a reason for every failure or delay. Advisory: not type-approved navigation equipment and not a navigation integrity service; no anti-spoofing performance is claimed</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>The official Galileo OSNMA test vectors published by the European GNSS Service Centre as an annex to the Receiver Guidelines (Test_vectors.zip, sha256 ef9b9afc6ef9e1c57393415cf2a1dc80c4035e7c06123907ea0bb97dd3ccf370): 18 of 18 sets, 186,382 tags authenticated, 0 failed, run offline on 2026-10-10 (evidence record in kshana-pro docs/evidence). Scope: the vectors validate the cryptographic verification (Merkle, KROOT/ECDSA, TESLA chain, MACK tags, ADKD 0/4/12) and its outcomes on the published scenarios; they use only HMAC-SHA-256, a SHA-256 chain, 128-bit keys, 40-bit tags and look-up entries 33 and 34, so CMAC-AES, SHA3-256 chains and other parameters are covered by published primitive known-answer tests and synthetic tests only. The trusted-time, data-binding, expiry and header-confirmation hardening is tested by the synthetic attack tests, not by an external oracle. Not checked: certificate revocation lists, live signals or a live receiver (the UBX word layout is checked on synthetic frames only), SHA3-256 Merkle trees, freshness without an independent time. Not an EU service</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/osnma_official_vectors.rs (opt-in, KSHANA_OSNMA_VECTORS: all 18 vector sets, 186,382 tags authenticated, 0 failed, per-set floors, chains announced, ADKD 0/4/12, alert verified, authentication resuming after…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st 