e or other phase</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/mission_thread_oracle.rs::the_stored_numbers_miss_the_registered_bars_as_recorded; tests/mission_thread_oracle.rs::the_diagnostic_places_the_miss_in_five_impulsive_events_not_in_the_force_model…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="quantum"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Cold-atom interferometer error terms: Raman laser-phase noise, wavefront-curvature bias and fringe-ambiguity resolution</span><code class="lg-mod">inertial::<wbr>cai_<wbr>error_<wbr>terms</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>inertial::cai_error_terms (library functions, not yet reachable from a scenario kind): the Raman-phase weighting function of a square-pulse three-pulse interferometer (Cheinet et al. 2008, Eq. 8) with the white-phase closed form (pi/2)^2 S_phi0/tau_R and a numeric route for any spectrum; the laser frequency noise the retro-reflection delay does not cancel (Le Gouet et al. 2007, Eqs. 9 to 11); the pure-defocus wavefront bias sigma_v^2/R of a thermal cloud and its reduction by a detection radius; the wrong-fringe-index probability erfc(pi/(sqrt(2) s)) for a classical-accelerometer aid and for two interrogation times, and its inverse</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Each closed form against an independent numerical route in the tests (frequency-domain quadrature of the exact transfer function and delay filter, a Monte Carlo over atoms for the wavefront bias, a Monte Carlo over shots for the fringe index) and its limiting cases. One published worked value: Cheinet et al. 2008 (arXiv:physics/0510197, Sec. IV) state that at tau_R = 20 us a white Raman phase noise below -111 dB rad^2/Hz is needed for 1 mrad per shot; the white term alone gives 0.99 mrad (the paper derives the level with its Eq. 17, flicker plus white). Internal consistency and one worked value, not an external validation; higher-order aberrations and any specific laser&#x27;s noise are not modelled</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>inertial::cai_error_terms::tests (raman_transfer_short_pulse_limit_matches_the_acceleration_transfer_function; white_raman_phase_closed_form_matches_quadrature; short_pulse_band_limited_closed_form_matches_quadrature…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">Greenhall and Riley exact equivalent degrees of freedom of the Allan, modified Allan and Hadamard variances</span><code class="lg-mod">allan <wbr>(edf_<wbr>greenhall,<wbr> <wbr>greenhall_<wbr>edf_<wbr>core); <wbr>assurance::<wbr>uncertainty <wbr>(edf)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>allan::edf_greenhall (with the edf_greenhall_adev, _mdev and _hdev wrappers): the full algorithm of Greenhall and Riley, Proc. 35th PTTI (2003), Section 3 (Eqns 7 to 13 and the large-J coefficients of Tables 1 to 3), for difference orders 1 to 3, noise exponents +2 to -4 wherever alpha + 2d &gt; 1, overlapping and non-overlapping, modified and unmodified estimators; NaN where it does not apply, including the unmodified white-PM case with ceil(M/S) &lt;= d, whose closed form is not implemented. assurance::uncertainty::edf now shares the code and keeps its outputs bit for bit</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>allantools 2024.6 ci.edf_greenhall, a third-party implementation of the published algorithm, run by scripts/gen_greenhall_edf_ref.py over the grid pre-registered in xval/greenhall-edf/PREREGISTRATION.md (committed alone, 696f68e6, before any comparison): at all 4 876 points where it returns a finite edf, kshana agrees within a relative 6.0e-13 (bar 1e-9); at its 46 NotImplementedError points kshana returns NaN; every case label occurs; the wrappers equal the core bit for bit; uncertainty::edf is bit-identical over 274 280 values (pinned as a SHA-256 before the refactor). At 32 points (alpha -4, d 3, unmodified, case 2.2) allantools fails in its Table 2 lookup, so they have no oracle value and are not counted. Stable32 was not run. 0.36 revision (docs/revisions/STUDIO15-greenhall-edf-portable.md): on portable maths the kernel takes its logarithm from a double-double evaluation rounded once (allan::greenhall_ln), and the unchanged Bar 1 holds again at all 4 876 points, worst relative 6.0e-13; the uncertainty::edf guard is re-based to the 0.36 portable dump (3 746 of the 274 280 values moved, at most 1.6e-12 relative, from the host-maths base)</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/greenhall_edf_allantools.rs (bars_1_to_3_against_allantools; bar_4_wrappers_equal_the_core); tests/greenhall_edf_no_moved_output.rs (uncertainty_edf_is_bit_identical_to_the_0_36_portable_baseline)…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Oscillator holdover presets from public datasheets</span><code class="lg-mod">telecom_<wbr>timing <wbr>(PRESETS,<wbr> <wbr>fit_<wbr>noise,<wbr> <wbr>with_<wbr>flicker_<wbr>floor,<wbr> <wbr>synthesize_<wbr>holdover); <wbr>models <wbr>(ClockModel)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Four presets — OCXO (Microchip OX-208), rubidium (Microchip 8040C), caesium (Microchip 5071A high-performance tube) and CSAC (Microchip SA.45s) — each carrying its datasheet&#x27;s Allan-deviation maxima, aging and temperature bound; a non-negative least-squares white + flicker + random-walk frequency-noise fit scaled to envelope every datasheet point, a flicker floor never below the longest-τ figure, linear aging and a sinusoidal temperature term, synthesised as a seeded holdover after a GNSS loss</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>The four named Microchip datasheets (document numbers and URLs in each preset and in docs/TELECOM-TIMING.md) for the input figures; the closed-form aging ramp and the fit&#x27;s envelope property as internal checks. How the figures become a noise model — the fit, the floor rule, the 30-day month, the linear temperature reading — is a modelling choice; no preset is a measurement of a unit. 0.30 round 2, one-sided bars against measured units (pre-registered 43d19980), a finding (stays MODELLED): the IGS station THU2 Symmetricom 8040C in ESA MGEX final clocks has an Allan deviation 0.35 to 0.87 of the rubidium preset but a holdover error 1.07 to 1.60 of it; the 5071A record sits outside the caesium preset to 1000 s (measurement white phase noise, 30x at 1 s) and in holdover (1.15 to 8.74); the worst 2011 production SA.45s is 1.26x the CSAC preset at 1 s; the OX-208 has no measured record (blocked)</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>telecom_timing::tests (every_preset_carries_a_named_datasheet_and_figures; the_noise_fit_envelopes_every_datasheet_point; pure_aging_matches_its_closed_form — the discrete aging ramp within 0.1 % of (1/2)·D·t² over a…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">Holdover prediction from a measured clock record, checked on held-out data</span><code class="lg-mod">slot_<wbr>timing <wbr>(ClockNoise::<wbr>from_<wbr>phase_<wbr>record,<wbr> <wbr>fit_<wbr>weighted,<wbr> <wbr>slot_<wbr>budget,<wbr> <wbr>breach_<wbr>after_<wbr>sync_<wbr>s)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>The <code>slot-timing</code> kind&#x27;s measured-record path: the overlapping Allan deviation of a phase record fitted by edf-weighted non-negative least squares in the white-phase and IEEE Std 1139 frequency-modulation basis (slot_timing::fit_weighted), then inverted for the coast time at which the time error reaches a threshold (slot_timing::slot_budget). The red-noise floor is measured from the record instead of assumed</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>A real free-running atomic clock: 556 990 one-second phase samples of a 5071A caesium standard measured against a hydrogen maser (A. Wallin, distributed with allantools; pinned commit an