span class="lg-req">NovAtel OEM7 ASCII and binary logs (BESTPOS, RANGE, RXSTATUS) for receiver-trust</span><code class="lg-mod">receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>machines::<wbr>novatel <wbr>(read_<wbr>novatel,<wbr> <wbr>novatel_<wbr>crc32); <wbr>receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>LogFormat::<wbr>Novatel</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Reads BESTPOS (position), RANGE (C/No per signal) and RXSTATUS (the receiver&#x27;s jammer flag, as the epoch&#x27;s self-report) from ASCII and binary OEM7 logs, CRC-checked, read-only (receiver_trust::machines::novatel).</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>None external as a pass bar. The field layouts and CRC follow the public OEM7 documentation (docs.novatel.com); the CRC routine was checked once against the CRC the documentation states for its own BESTPOSA example (cited, not quoted). Fixtures are self-written; no log from a real receiver was read</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>receiver_trust::machines::novatel::tests (pinned CRC, ASCII and binary records, bad CRC skipped, hostile input); tests/receiver_trust_machines.rs::novatel_jammer_flag_reaches_the_receiver_self_report</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="integrity"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">RTCM 3 MSM4 and MSM7 carrier-to-noise reader for receiver-trust</span><code class="lg-mod">receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>machines::<wbr>rtcm3 <wbr>(read_<wbr>rtcm3,<wbr> <wbr>crc24q); <wbr>receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>LogFormat::<wbr>Rtcm3</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Reads the C/N0 of every signal cell of RTCM 3 MSM4 and MSM7 messages (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, SBAS, QZSS, BeiDou, NavIC) from a frame stream, CRC-24Q checked (receiver_trust::machines::rtcm3). Layouts from the BSD-licensed pyrtcm tables, not from the RTCM standard text.</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>ReferenceImpl in a one-off check, not a test in the suite: pyrtcm 1.2.0&#x27;s decoder reads the same self-written frames to the same C/N0 and epoch time. It shares its tables&#x27; source with this reader, so it checks the bit handling, not the layout. No capture from a real receiver or base station was read</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>receiver_trust::machines::rtcm3::tests (CRC-24Q catalogue check value, MSM4/MSM7 C/N0 and epoch merging, GLONASS time and SBAS id mapping, bad CRC and other messages)</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">GNSS-SDR monitor adapter for receiver-trust</span><code class="lg-mod">receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>machines::<wbr>gnss_<wbr>sdr <wbr>(read_<wbr>gnss_<wbr>sdr_<wbr>monitor); <wbr>receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>LogFormat::<wbr>GnssSdr</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Reads GNSS-SDR Monitor (Gnss_Synchro) and PVT-monitor messages, relayed to JSON lines with the proto field names, into per-channel C/N0, fix, satellites used, HDOP and sky (receiver_trust::machines::gnss_sdr; integrations/gnss-sdr/relay.py).</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>None external: field names come from the GNSS-SDR documentation; neither the reader nor relay.py was run against a live GNSS-SDR or a real capture</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>receiver_trust::machines::gnss_sdr::tests; integrations/gnss-sdr/example.jsonl</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">IMU log ingest, gyro heading input and Allan fit of hybrid sensor parameters</span><code class="lg-mod">receiver_<wbr>trust::<wbr>machines::<wbr>imu,<wbr> <wbr>imu_<wbr>fit; <wbr>surface::<wbr>imu_<wbr>fit; <wbr>scenario <wbr>[log.imu]</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Reads an IMU CSV (documented columns, or the EuRoC layout); integrates the yaw rate into the heading the heading-course monitor reads ([log.imu]); and fits the accelerometer and gyro noise parameters of the hybrid and