inal 15 min SP3 of 2025-02-24 vs the IGS final 30 s clocks, 32 GPS satellites: node median |Δ| 2.6e-13 s; 3038 mid-point records RMS 0.121 ns, p95 0.265 ns; holding the node instead…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Carrier-phase tightly coupled GNSS/INS with float ambiguities</span><code class="lg-mod">fusion::<wbr>carrier_<wbr>tc <wbr>(run_<wbr>carrier_<wbr>tc,<wbr> <wbr>CarrierTcCfg),<wbr> <wbr>fusion::<wbr>trajectory <wbr>(truth_<wbr>epochs)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Error-state EKF over 15 INS states, a two-state receiver clock and one float carrier ambiguity per tracked satellite; pseudorange, carrier phase and optional range rate from an SGP4 Walker constellation (light-time and Sagnac), Klobuchar and Saastamoinen/Niell corrections applied in the loop at the filter&#x27;s own position; time-differenced-carrier slip detection with a per-satellite threshold widened by the velocity uncertainty; ambiguity re-initialisation on slips and re-acquisition</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Internal consistency: the measurements are synthesised from the models the filter uses (χ² NEES/NIS over seeds, a noise-free convergence, slip injection). MODELLED; no real receiver data or third-party filter is compared</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/fusion_carrier_tc.rs (figure-8 drive: steady 3-D RMS 0.025 m carrier vs 0.470 m code on identical measurements; 12 seeds mean NIS/dof 1.00 and steady NEES/dof 0.92; a 1-cycle slip detected at its epoch with no…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">GNSS/INS maritime, rail and aviation packs with a tight-coupling option</span><code class="lg-mod">fusion::<wbr>pack <wbr>(TightCfg,<wbr> <wbr>[tight]),<wbr> <wbr>scenarios <wbr><span class="nw">gnss-ins-maritime </span><wbr>/<wbr>